{"h":3395,"w":2400,"lines":[{"x":0.77160493914987061,"y":0.046511627815782663,"c":0.30000001192092896,"h":0.008720930389296444,"t":"1718867188","w":0.069958845774332645},{"t":"READING","h":0.017754724365521946,"x":0.42794172292517468,"y":0.094320312196146894,"c":1,"w":0.12971326192220051},{"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","h":0.016195524146054296,"c":1,"x":0.10082304364134179,"y":0.15253239096150795,"w":0.28806584676106772},{"c":1,"x":0.10279087703544007,"y":0.18666492490872533,"h":0.019111953438802676,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","w":0.76147837320963541},{"x":0.10082304606459527,"c":1,"w":0.16049382527669273,"t":"Passage 1 below.","h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.20494186032104278},{"w":0.24485595703124996,"t":"Bats to the rescue","h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1,"x":0.37037037519330995,"y":0.23969375737294374},{"x":0.23662551048245406,"w":0.51234568277994785,"h":0.01598837125708541,"t":"How Madagascar's bats are helping to save the rainforest","c":1,"y":0.27616279095575957},{"w":0.77366251627604177,"x":0.10082306310683511,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"t":"There are few places in the world where relations between agriculture and conservation are more","y":0.30948174349768653},{"w":0.74897120157877606,"c":1,"h":0.016015764400450827,"t":"strained. Madagascar's forests are being converted to agricultural land at a rate of one percent","x":0.10082304107183508,"y":0.32703488357461508},{"c":1,"x":0.10082304298513994,"y":0.34302325566711689,"w":0.7366255187988282,"t":"every year. Much of this destruction is fuelled by the cultivation of the country's main staple","h":0.01598837238037687},{"w":0.76761032104492188,"t":"crop: rice. And a key reason for this destruction is that insect pests are destroying vast quantities","h":0.01868901516720034,"c":1,"x":0.10076767611805414,"y":0.35807870450645574},{"y":0.37632508816718979,"x":0.10082305646712834,"w":0.75925923665364581,"c":1,"t":"of what is grown by local subsistence farmers, leading them to clear forest to create new paddy","h":0.016195524146054185},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"x":0.10082304296418793,"c":1,"t":"fields. The result is devastating habitat and biodiversity loss on the island, but not all species","y":0.39389534870451171,"w":0.7366255187988282},{"w":0.75308639526367183,"h":0.01598837238037687,"y":0.40988372078414059,"c":1,"t":"are suffering. In fact, some of the island's insectivorous bats are currently thriving and this has","x":0.10082305741397855},{"c":1,"y":0.42726737344292376,"h":0.013250883392226132,"w":0.49588475545247401,"x":0.10082305426608486,"t":"important implications for farmers and conservationists alike."},{"c":1,"w":0.74691360473632806,"x":0.10082303288102698,"t":"Enter University of Cambridge zoologist Ricardo Rocha. He's passionate about conservation,","y":0.45930232543466731,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"w":0.7366255187988282,"x":0.098765429801378174,"t":"and bats. More specifically, he's interested in how bats are responding to human activity and","y":0.47673733776837213,"h":0.01454173212759069,"c":1},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"w":0.72222223917643225,"y":0.4926383981000102,"t":"deforestation in particular. Rocha's new study shows that several species of bats are giving","x":0.10082303668446911},{"t":"Madagascar's rice farmers a vital pest control service by feasting on plagues of insects. And this,","y":0.50872093049064326,"w":0.77366251627604166,"h":0.016014051942858987,"c":1,"x":0.10082307009243172},{"x":0.10288066399030782,"w":0.62962961832682296,"y":0.52616279057775939,"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"t":"he believes, can ease the financial pressure on farmers to turn forest into fields."},{"w":0.77777776082356764,"x":0.10082305363976236,"c":1,"t":"Bats comprise roughly one-fifth of all mammal species in Madagascar and thirty-six recorded bat","h":0.014723203769140158,"y":0.55948174314698762},{"x":0.10075882877664023,"t":"species are native to the island, making it one of the most important regions for conservation of","y":0.57359699320703439,"h":0.019174048982042891,"c":1,"w":0.7634766642252605},{"x":0.098670316549610823,"c":1,"w":0.33351687113444012,"h":0.016883082889696199,"y":0.59149301913311014,"t":"this animal group anywhere in the world."},{"x":0.10070238919795098,"h":0.020476728783058173,"t":"Co-leading an international team of scientists, Rocha found that several species of indigenous","y":0.62358081070636939,"w":0.74917455037434899,"c":1},{"y":0.64098837231113737,"w":0.75308639526367194,"t":"bats are taking advantage of habitat modification to hunt insects swarming above the country's","x":0.10082306651425445,"c":1,"h":0.015988371257085632},{"t":"rice fields. They include the Malagasy mouse-eared bat, Major's long-fingered bat, the Malagasy","y":0.65842167237070048,"h":0.015996932421752819,"c":1,"w":0.76954732259114589,"x":0.10082304641894088},{"y":0.67267024827736743,"w":0.47350657145182296,"h":0.018156763802428366,"t":"white-bellied free-tailed bat and Peters' wrinkle-lipped bat.","c":1,"x":0.10071869266129899},{"t":"'These winner species are providing a valuable free service to Madagascar as biological pest","x":0.10288065611768768,"w":0.73662551879882809,"h":0.014534883982160851,"y":0.7078488370763043,"c":1},{"x":0.10283498208644308,"y":0.72336047680737314,"t":"suppressors,' says Rocha. 'We found that six species of bat are preying on rice pests, including the","c":1,"h":0.016728907788459702,"w":0.78198532104492191},{"w":0.76337448120117191,"c":1,"y":0.74116607776200583,"h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.10288066050687215,"t":"paddy swarming caterpillar and grass webworm. The damage which these insects cause puts the"},{"w":0.65030390421549478,"h":0.015730423697032481,"t":"island's farmers under huge financial pressure and that encourages deforestation.'","c":1,"x":0.10078986662049004,"y":0.75724399773515561},{"x":0.10082305109832362,"t":"The study, now published in the journal Agriculture, Ecosystems and Environment, set out to","y":0.79063604264806753,"w":0.73868311564127609,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1},{"w":0.76131688435872391,"h":0.01472320376914027,"c":1,"x":0.098765426027344463,"y":0.80800942279613042,"t":"investigate the feeding activity of insectivorous bats in the farmland bordering the Ranomafana"},{"t":"National Park in the southeast of the country.","x":0.10273313519889792,"y":0.8219005402645968,"w":0.36249501546223956,"h":0.016901280208807767,"c":1},{"y":0.86773255795657411,"w":0.022633744875590001,"x":0.85802469125562064,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"81"},{"c":1,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","y":0.95314993796778535,"h":0.03375352650564889,"w":0.30612678527832038,"x":0.66991655033568553}]}